  "step_3": "The decision reason hinges on comparing the maximum probability of each lottery, which in this case clearly favors Lottery A (100% vs. 66%). However, the individual does not mention certainty, maximum probability, or the structural feature of one lottery being certain. Instead, the focus is on the 100 Euro difference and its likelihood (2/3), interpreted as not compelling enough to justify choosing the risky option. This suggests a consideration of expected value or perceived insignificance of the gain under risk, rather than a focus on the highest probability outcome per se. There is no evidence that the individual identified or used the maximum probability as a decision rule. Therefore, while the individual may have chosen Lottery A (implied by downplaying the risky gain), the reasoning does not align with the specified decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 20
}

